<!--
  Environment for contour following with force feedback, for mujoco_robotsimulator_crospi.

  A table with a hollow circular contour on top of it: a ring-shaped wall whose INNER face is a circle of
  diameter 0.35 m (radius 0.175) centered at (0.174, -0.615) in the world, 8 cm high, on the table top (z = 0.15).
  Designed for the UR10e with the cylindrical contact tool (urdf/ur10e_cylinder_tool.urdf: 15 cm long, 3 cm diameter,
  fixed to tool0) pointing down. At the joints [4.7116, -1.5708, 2.0944, -2.0944, -1.5708, 0] the tool tip is at
  (0.174, -0.615, 0.241), i.e. right above the center of the contour, 9 cm above the table. Intended sequence:
    1. move down (-z) into the ring until contact with the table top (z = 0.15)
    2. move radially (any direction in the xy plane) until contact with the inner face of the ring
       (the tool axis is then at 0.160 m from the center)
    3. follow the contour (tangential motion) while regulating the normal (radial) contact force
  The whole contour is reachable with the tool pointing down (checked with the UR10e: inverse kinematics along the
  contour within the joint limits, far from singularities).

  The ring is made of 180 box segments (MuJoCo replaces concave meshes by their convex hull, so a single ring mesh
  cannot be used). Their inner faces form a regular 180-gon with apothem 0.175: the deviation from the circle is
  at most 0.03 mm, with a change of direction of 2 degrees between facets.
  The outer face (diameter 0.41 m) can also be used for contour following from the outside.
  This file was generated with a script (ring segments: pos = (r cos a, r sin a), euler = (0, 0, a)).

  All coordinates are in the world frame of the simulation (with the identity base pose of the simulator
  configuration, world = robot base_link).

  Sensors (published by the simulator on <topic_namespace>/mujoco_sensors/<name>):
    - table_touch:   normal contact force [N] on the table top
    - contour_touch: normal contact force [N] on the ring (inner or outer face)
    - contour_center: ground-truth position of the center of the contour at the table top [m]

  The physics options (timestep, gravity, integrator, contacts) are set by the simulator configuration.
-->
<mujoco model="table_with_circular_contour">
  <compiler angle="radian"/>

  <visual>
    <headlight ambient="0.4 0.4 0.4" diffuse="0.6 0.6 0.6"/>
  </visual>

  <asset>
    <texture name="grid" type="2d" builtin="checker" rgb1="0.2 0.3 0.4" rgb2="0.3 0.4 0.5" width="512" height="512"/>
    <material name="grid" texture="grid" texrepeat="4 4" reflectance="0.1"/>
    <material name="wood" rgba="0.55 0.4 0.3 1"/>
    <material name="steel" rgba="0.6 0.62 0.65 1" specular="0.6" shininess="0.6"/>
  </asset>

  <default>
    <!-- Rigid, static contact surfaces for force control during sliding:
         - priority 1: these contact parameters are used (instead of mixing them with those of the robot geoms);
         - solref timeconst 0.02 s, critically damped, and solimp 0.9-0.95 (MuJoCo defaults): stiff contact (about
           0.01 mm penetration at 10 N) that is still compliant enough to avoid force chattering while sliding along
           the contour (a stiffer contact, e.g. solref 0.005, makes the instantaneous contact force jump between 0 and
           2x its mean value);
         - friction: moderate sliding friction (0.3) so that the tool can slide along the contour while pressing on it,
           small torsional and rolling friction;
         - condim 3: normal force + 2D tangential friction. -->
    <default class="rigid_surface">
      <geom priority="1" condim="3" friction="0.3 0.005 0.0001" solref="0.02 1" solimp="0.9 0.95 0.001 0.5 2"/>
    </default>
  </default>

  <worldbody>
    <light name="top" pos="0 0 3" dir="0 0 -1" directional="true"/>
    <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="0 0 0.05" material="grid"/>

    <!-- Table: 0.8 x 0.7 m, top surface at z = 0.15 m, centered at (0.174, -0.615) -->
    <body name="table" pos="0.174 -0.615 0.075">
      <geom name="table_top" class="rigid_surface" type="box" size="0.4 0.35 0.075" material="wood"/>
      <!-- Touch volume of the table top (invisible, non-colliding) -->
      <site name="table_top_surface" type="box" pos="0 0 0.075" size="0.4 0.35 0.005" group="4" rgba="0 1 0 0.2"/>

